<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  The H-1B list build (#252): daily at 06:50, after the 06:30 sources job, rewrite companies.md and unsure.md in
  `<store folder>/h1b/` from the USCIS files already on disk, so a company added since the last build gets its line
  (or "No H-1B on record" stays true). It reads the store read only and sends no request. The files are written whole
  or not at all (a temp file renamed over the old one), so the job list and the Outbox never read half a file.
  confirmed.md, his hand written answers, is read and never written.

  The USCIS input is locked (sources/h1b-uscis/h1b_hub_fy2022-2026.csv); with no CSV the run exits 1 and leaves the
  old files. A new USCIS export is a manual step: replace the file, and the next run picks it up.

  StartCalendarInterval (not StartInterval), so a run missed while the Mac sleeps fires on wake. A rerun is safe.

  It follows the deploy tool's one convention (#17, outreach/deploy/jobs.py): WorkingDirectory is the live checkout,
  the program is the checkout's venv python run as a module, and both streams go to the log. Placeholders, filled by
  the deploy tool: {{LIVE_CHECKOUT}} is the live checkout, {{LOG_PATH}} the log file. Nothing else is filled; the
  store is the default.

  Not installed by the repo, and never loaded from a worktree. Installing it goes through the deploy tool
  (python -m outreach.deploy plan, then install). To remove it:
    launchctl bootout gui/$(id -u)/com.devanshu.outreach-h1b
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>com.devanshu.outreach-h1b</string>
  <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
  <string>{{LIVE_CHECKOUT}}</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>{{LIVE_CHECKOUT}}/.venv/bin/python</string>
    <string>-m</string>
    <string>outreach.h1b</string>
    <string>build</string>
  </array>
  <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
  <dict>
    <key>Hour</key>
    <integer>6</integer>
    <key>Minute</key>
    <integer>50</integer>
  </dict>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>{{LOG_PATH}}</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>{{LOG_PATH}}</string>
</dict>
</plist>
